{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Mer De Noms feels like a natural next choice after 10.000 Days because I am especially drawn to atmospheric heaviness with melody right now.",
    "The Sickness builds directly on my recent interest in Ten Thousand Fists, while City of Evil connects with the melodic metal and elaborate guitar work I enjoy in In Flames."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "S&M shares the heavy sound of my listening history, but its live orchestral approach does not fit my current preference for focused studio material.",
    "Reign In Blood fits my heavier interests, but intensity alone is less compelling to me right now than heaviness paired with melody."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to treat a shared heavy sound as enough to make albums equally appealing, although atmosphere, melody, and recording style affect what I choose.",
    "Recommending several related albums assumes I want to explore them all immediately; I would choose The Sickness before adding Believe on this visit."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent interest in Tool makes atmospheric, melodic heavy rock particularly timely, which is why Mer De Noms stands out most.",
    "An album can fit my taste without being an immediate choice: Hybrid Theory, Meteora, and Saturate appeal to me, but have less pull than my three selections today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understand my interest in heavy music, but only some capture the melody, atmosphere, and immediate curiosity driving my choices now."
}"}
